    "off": 378001,
    "end": 378385,
    "text": "Note.— With the exception of the original commissioned oflicers, the resi- dences of the men composing this company can no where be found by me. I know, however, that they were all from Cherokee and Macon counties and others ■of the extreme west end of the State, Berry, J. D., e. June 18th, '61.",
    "tokens": 54,
    "co": "A"
   },
   {
    "off": 428377,
    "end": 428600,
    "text": "Note.— This company was constituted by naen of the counties of Wilson and Nash, but with the few exceptions given above I am unable to -say to which of the two shires the individuals belonged.",
    "tokens": 35,
    "co": "E"
   },
   {
    "off": 433835,
    "end": 433987,
    "text": "Note.— This company was not reported in the Roll of Honor, and only the above meagre record is to be had from the Archives Office.",
